00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
hi uh today i'm going to be talking  about why exactly i have a second  brain if you're new here welcome my name  is elizabeth i'm a medical student and  an artist living  in london and i am a consumer of a lot  of information  through my university degree books that  i try to read on the side  and other courses that i like to do i  feel  as though i am in a constant state of  forgetting things  this was all until i created my second  brain  this is a term which i love coined by  thiago forte it's basically a glorified  information management slash note-taking  system honestly it is one of the best  things i have done in my life  i wish i could give this speech to  myself  five years ago it would absolutely have  changed things for me  completely my second brain is basically  a highly organized collection  of everything that i consume which is  all explained  categorized and connected with one  another in this way  i have a much more intelligent easily  accessible  and organized version of myself which i  can access  whenever i feel the need to work on  something or  even just for fun in this video i will  explain six reasons why  i believe that being very intentional  with your note-taking and information  management is  absolutely critical so let's get  straight into it the first reason  is investing in your future memory i am  a firm believer that  it is my own personal responsibility to  set my future  self up for as much success happiness  and joy as possible so i am very often  working with my future self in mind i  recognize that my future self  may have projects and may also be quite  lazy and procrastinating when she has to  do them  so i prepare a system with a huge  backlog for her  so that she is never starting from a  blank page but  always has highly processed information  the next reason  is information overload in building a  second brain  thiago puts up a slide where he showed  that the average person  consumes the equivalent of 174  newspapers of information a day and this  is the average person if you're watching  this video  which means you're probably similar to  me we're consuming maybe double or  triple this amount and therefore this is  what makes me think that maybe  i don't have a very bad memory but it's  just impossible  for me to keep up with everything that  is being thrown at me  all the time in a similar way that i  will summarize my lectures into one or  two lines  to be able to remember at the very least  just that  i will do the same thing with whole  books or  chapters of a book or even a sentence in  a book that i find is very very  important and i will add this  to my notes the next reason is the view  that you are the average of the five  projects that you are spending the most  of your time on  i love this because when i was younger  my parents would always tell me that  i was the average of the five people  that i spent the most of my time with  even though  as adults we can be quite intentional to  some extent with the people that we  surround ourselves  i don't think that we can exactly do the  same thing when it comes to information  for example even googling things will  show up different results for different  people  we are really at the mercy of algorithms  on youtube for example or  on instagram feed i have very little  control as to what information i am  being exposed to  however when it comes to the things that  i am spending hours or even  weeks or days considering and processing  in my  second brain these are things that i can  choose by myself and be very  intentional about i try to make these  things are highly intellectually  stimulating or very  inspiring or things that i am passionate  about and especially  things that i hope one day will also be  helpful to other people and that i can  share and improve  more people's lives with so you can  choose whatever these values are for you  and be a lot more intentional with them  in your second brain than you are  in just consuming information from  everywhere the next reason is that  sometimes i will be exposed to things  which in the moment  i don't really feel like paying  attention to but which i know will be  very important in the future  or the opposite of this for example i've  always been very passionate about art  but because i thought that i couldn't  see how it would fit into my life as a  doctor i kind of ignored  taking notes on art for a very large  part of my life  which now i regret so much because i  finally have been given a platform  where i can talk about things that i was  passionate in and if only i had  more notes on art that process would  have been a lot easier so i would say  you never really know where your life  goes and if you're very passionate about  something  chances are consciously or  subconsciously you are creating  situations wherein  in the future you will be able to do  that thing this has definitely been the  case for me so i feel as though we  should not trust our energy levels and  situation  right now but rather we should trust our  passions if something makes me really  excited  i will make note of it regardless of  what topic it is on because chances are  i will be needing it in the future  the next idea is that brains are for  making connections  and not storing information this is  something that has been  revolutionary for me i feel as though  when i started medicine  i was paying so much attention to  focusing on very very small details  i feel as though i did not have a strong  command of  the bigger picture and i think this  bigger picture thinking  is much more valuable as humans i don't  think we're very good at  memorizing large amounts of information  and because i have a second brain where  all those details are stored in  i don't really need to care that much  because i know that they exist and i  know where to find them  so my brain is emptied and free to  rather come up with creative things  and to make connections between them and  to look them up  when i need those things to be done my  last point and perhaps the most  important one  is that building a second brain is a  system  that gets better the more you fail  let me explain this a bit i always used  to be  a huge fan of creating very detailed  systems about things  and recently i have started accounting  for  those systems failing because that is  absolutely  guaranteed i know for sure that there  will be times where i am lazy  and tired and procrastinating and not  sticking to my schedules  so now my schedules are optimized  for my lazy version rather than my  productive version of myself in the end  of the day i think  enjoying what you do is the most  important thing so honestly i want to  feel as good  when i am lounging about doing nothing  and avoiding my work  as when i am actually doing the work  this is how i create systems in my life  i will definitely  go into a lot more detail about this in  explaining how my second brain works  but basically if i capture something  before i  block it into its categories the longer  i leave it as a draft  be less a day a week six months the  longer my brain will have to  subconsciously simmer on that concept  and i find that when i come back to  categorizing my drafts for months and  months ago i've created a lot more  novel connections in my notes rather  than the ones that i thought initially i  would put them in on the very first day  so this is the system that gets better  the lazier you are  which for me is absolutely brilliant  these are my reasons  why as a professional in the modern  world because i am consuming so much  information  i need to be equally or if not more  careful intentional and organized about  what i do  with everything that i consume and i  have found that building a second brain  has been honestly the most life-changing  satisfying  and brilliant things that i've ever done  in regards to information processing in  my life  i'm honestly very very excited to share  more details around this  my system is in notion but i'm sure that  it can be done  on many different platforms if you made  it so far that's great  you are definitely my type of person  thank you so much for spending this time  with me i hope you have a wonderful rest  of your day  be kind yourself and others and don't  believe everything you think thanks  bye  [Music]

